  "The page number «246» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it. The page has no signature. Two columns divided by a vertical rule, as on pp. [241]-245 (JP2 0275-0279), transcribed column by column: the left column L01-L50, the right L51-L95; the letter heads «T.» (L17), «U.» (L59), «W.» (L65), «Y.» (L84) and «Z.» (L86) in bold, centred in their columns, each after a blank line; each entry begins at the edge of its column, its further lines indented. The entry «Zich» continues on p. 247 (JP2 0281).",
  "L49 and L54: the fractions are built up, «1» over «60³» and over «60²», the exponents raised, written {fr:NUMERATOR|DENOMINATOR}. The semicolons of L08, L09, L13, L18, L19, L28, L30, L32, L66, L67, L79 and L93 stand after a thin space (8-11 px); written with a space. L27: a speck after the point of «T. 91.» (3 px against the 6 px of the point); not transcribed. «Shāh» (L94) in spaced roman. The dashes are long (31-47 px), except in «T. 6—8» (L77), which is printed as a short dash with a space on each side (27 px); written —.",
  "Checked against the text, for example: «Shemeli» on pp. 13, 16, 18 and 29 (JP2 0045, 0048, 0050, 0061), «filshohor» of C and «filsohor» of M in the apparatus of Tab. 9 (p. 120, JP2 0152), «Tezwiet» on p. 25 and in the title of Tab. 79 (p. 194, JP2 0226), «felek eltedewir» in the apparatus of Tab. 9 (note 20), «Thuld» and the «thuid» of C and M on p. 9 (JP2 0041, the text and note 7), «delidhe», «thelidhe» and «thelidae» in the apparatus of p. 15 (JP2 0047), where the glossary has «Thelide», «Thelidhe» and «Delidhe» (p. 242, JP2 0276, L56), «Wakhod mebibelche» in note 18 of p. 27 (JP2 0059), «Tarbea», «Tethlith» and «Tezdiz» in the heads of Tab. 91 (p. 206, JP2 0238). The ordinal fractions «Thenia» (seconds), «Thelitha» (thirds) and «Rabia» (fourths, p. 245, JP2 0279, L64-L67) are the multiples of 1/60², 1/60³ and 1/60⁴."
